 "text": "Hi, how are you doing now? Tent poles are usually long enough that each end can go at corners, and the middle over center pole. Which part are you most worried about? Then that's probably the spot. Set the tree tent legs there, and use guy ropes to pull the tent out if it pulls hard. That can happen if you set it around a tree that's been cut for a light pole. You can usually save it by cutting in fresh branches. That's a nice spot too, right near the fire. Just keep the tent poles out of the hottest spot. Good. Set it up and enjoy the views. If it's windy, use all the guy ropes and clip the tent pegs tight.",
